{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,25]],"date-time":"2026-10-25T19:24:17Z","timestamp":1792956257980,"version":"4.5.0"},"reference-count":13,"publisher":"Wiley","issue":"9","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2007,3,23]],"date-time":"2007-03-23T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1174608000000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":7751,"URL":"http:\/\/onlinelibrary.wiley.com\/termsAndConditions#vor"}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":["Electron. Comm. Jpn. Pt. I"],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[1986,1]]},"abstract":"<jats:title>Abstract<\/jats:title>\n                  <jats:p>\n                    In the (\n                    <jats:italic>k, n<\/jats:italic>\n                    ) threshold scheme, the information\n                    <jats:italic>X<\/jats:italic>\n                    is partitioned and coded into subinformation. If any\n                    <jats:italic>k<\/jats:italic>\n                    subinformation is obtained among\n                    <jats:italic>n<\/jats:italic>\n                    subinformation, the original information\n                    <jats:italic>X<\/jats:italic>\n                    can be recovered completely. However, no information can be obtained at all concerning\n                    <jats:italic>X<\/jats:italic>\n                    from any (\n                    <jats:italic>k<\/jats:italic>\n                    \u2013 1) subinformation. Thus, the (\n                    <jats:italic>k, n<\/jats:italic>\n                    ) threshold scheme is suited to the distributed storage or transmission of information. On the other hand, each subinformation requires the same number of bits as the original information\n                    <jats:italic>X<\/jats:italic>\n                    , which is very inefficient from the viewpoint of the coding efficiency. This paper extends the (\n                    <jats:italic>k, n<\/jats:italic>\n                    ) threshold scheme and proposes the (\n                    <jats:italic>k, L, n<\/jats:italic>\n                    ) threshold scheme. In the proposed scheme, the original information can be recovered completely from any\n                    <jats:italic>k<\/jats:italic>\n                    subinformation, but no information concerning\n                    <jats:italic>X<\/jats:italic>\n                    is obtained at all from any (\n                    <jats:italic>k<\/jats:italic>\n                    \u2013\n                    <jats:italic>L<\/jats:italic>\n                    ) subinformation. From any (\n                    <jats:italic>k<\/jats:italic>\n                    \u2013\n                    <jats:italic>t<\/jats:italic>\n                    ) subinformation (1 \u2264\n                    <jats:italic>t<\/jats:italic>\n                    \u2264\n                    <jats:italic>L<\/jats:italic>\n                    \u2013 1), the information obtained for\n                    <jats:italic>X<\/jats:italic>\n                    contains the ambiguity of (\n                    <jats:italic>t\/L<\/jats:italic>\n                    )\n                    <jats:italic>H<\/jats:italic>\n                    (\n                    <jats:italic>X<\/jats:italic>\n                    ). In (\n                    <jats:italic>k, L, n<\/jats:italic>\n                    ) scheme, the bit\u2010length of each subinformation is 1\/\n                    <jats:italic>L<\/jats:italic>\n                    of the information\n                    <jats:italic>X<\/jats:italic>\n                    , which is a coding with very high efficiency. This paper presents a construction method for (\n                    <jats:italic>k, L, n<\/jats:italic>\n                    ) threshold scheme, together with the discussion of its characteristics.\n                  <\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1002\/ecja.4410690906","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2007,7,13]],"date-time":"2007-07-13T10:16:27Z","timestamp":1184321787000},"page":"46-54","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":101,"title":["Secret sharing system using (k, L, n) threshold scheme"],"prefix":"10.1002","volume":"69","author":[{"given":"Hirosuke","family":"Yamamoto","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"311","published-online":{"date-parts":[[2007,3,23]]},"reference":[{"key":"e_1_2_1_2_2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1145\/359168.359176"},{"key":"e_1_2_1_3_2","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1145\/358746.358762"},{"key":"e_1_2_1_4_2","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"1","DOI":"10.1109\/TIT.1983.1056621","article-title":"On secret sharing systems","volume":"29","author":"Karnin E. D.","year":"1983","journal-title":"I. E. E. E. Trans. Inf. Theory"},{"key":"e_1_2_1_5_2","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"2","DOI":"10.1109\/TIT.1983.1056651","article-title":"A modular approach to key safeguarding","volume":"29","author":"Asmuth C.","year":"1983","journal-title":"I. E. E. E. Trans. Inf. Theory"},{"key":"e_1_2_1_6_2","article-title":"A study of secret sharing systems using algebraic error\u2010correcting codes","volume":"84","author":"Matsumi","year":"1984","journal-title":"Tech. Rep. I. E. C. E., Japan"},{"key":"e_1_2_1_7_2","unstructured":"Matsumi Tokiwa KasaharaandNamekawa. Notes on (K N) threshold scheme 67th Symp. on Inf. Theory and Its Appl. pp.158\u2013163(Nov.1984)."},{"key":"e_1_2_1_8_2","article-title":"On stone code","volume":"84","author":"Yamaguchi","year":"1984","journal-title":"Tech. Rep. I. E. C. E., Japan"},{"key":"e_1_2_1_9_2","unstructured":"YamaguchiandImai A decoding method for stone codes and its applications 7th Symp. on Inf. Theory and Appl. pp.36\u201340(Nov.1984)."},{"key":"e_1_2_1_10_2","first-page":"2","article-title":"Sharing Cryptographic Keys in Multigroup and Its Analysis","volume":"22","author":"Koyama K.","year":"1981","journal-title":"Trans. Inf. Proc. Soc. Jap."},{"key":"e_1_2_1_11_2","first-page":"1","article-title":"Cryptographic key sharing methods for multigroups and security analysis","volume":"66","author":"Koyama K.","year":"1983","journal-title":"Trans. I. E. C. E., Japan (Section E)"},{"key":"e_1_2_1_12_2","first-page":"3","article-title":"File management system by k\u2010out\u2010of\u2010 N individual identification","volume":"25","author":"Matsui K.","year":"1984","journal-title":"Trans. Inf. Proc. Soc. Jap."},{"key":"e_1_2_1_13_2","unstructured":"H.Yamamoto. On secret sharing communication systems with two or three channels I. E. E. E. Trans. Inf. Theory (to be published)."},{"key":"e_1_2_1_14_2","first-page":"1","article-title":"Multiple\u2010burst error correction with the Chinese remainder theorem","volume":"11","author":"Stone J. J.","year":"1963","journal-title":"J. SIAM"}],"container-title":["Electronics and Communications in Japan (Part I: Communications)"],"original-title":[],"language":"en","link":[{"URL":"https:\/\/api.wiley.com\/onlinelibrary\/tdm\/v1\/articles\/10.1002%2Fecja.4410690906","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"text-mining"},{"URL":"https:\/\/onlinelibrary.wiley.com\/doi\/pdf\/10.1002\/ecja.4410690906","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2023,10,21]],"date-time":"2023-10-21T09:36:42Z","timestamp":1697881002000},"score":1,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/onlinelibrary.wiley.com\/doi\/10.1002\/ecja.4410690906"}},"subtitle":[],"short-title":[],"issued":{"date-parts":[[1986,1]]},"references-count":13,"journal-issue":{"issue":"9","published-print":{"date-parts":[[1986,1]]}},"alternative-id":["10.1002\/ecja.4410690906"],"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1002\/ecja.4410690906","archive":["Portico"],"relation":{},"ISSN":["8756-6621","1520-6424"],"issn-type":[{"value":"8756-6621","type":"print